[2026-07-19T11:21:54.868Z] [INFO]   "summary": "Here's the map.\n\n## 1. Web search / web fetch tool definitions and execution\n\n**Definition (advertised tool schemas)** — `/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784459807581/src/agentic_coding/driver.rs`\n- `DRIVER_TOOLS: [&str; 4] = [\"web_search\", \"web_fetch\", \"write_file\", \"run_command\"]` (line 34)\n- `tool_definitions(names)` (line 240) — OpenAI-shaped function schemas\n- `tool_description(name)` (line 251) — `web_search` takes `{\"query\": string}`, `web_fetch` takes `{\"url\": string}`\n\n**Execution** — `driver.rs:216 execute_tool_call(call, workspace)` dispatches by name to `corpus::web_search(...)` / `corpus::web_fetch(...)`.\n\n**Actual implementations** — `/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784459807581/src/agentic_coding/corpus.rs`\n- `web_search(query) -> String` (line 81): keyword match over an in-memory `pages()` corpus, emits ranked `N. title / url / snippet…` lines. Returns `web_search: no results for {query:?}` on miss.\n- `web_fetch(url) -> String` (line 112): exact-URL lookup in the same corpus; unknown URL returns `web_fetch error: 404 not found for {url}`.\n- Important: **this is an offline deterministic corpus, not the network.** The module doc (lines 1-11) is explicit — CI has no network and the repo's determinism stance forbids live calls. `pages()` (line 33) is the fisherman-tale page plus one Wikidata-lexeme page per entry in `meaning_detail::CONCEPTS`.\n\n**Client-side argument shaping** — `planner.rs:905 fetch_arguments(url)` emits `{\"url\":…, \"format\":\"text\"}` (multi-CLI compatibility; see doc comment lines 891-904). `write_arguments` at line 883 does the same trick with `path`/`filePath`/`file_path`.\n\n**Separate, non-agentic search stack** — `/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784459807581/src/web_search_core.rs` (`no_std`+alloc, mirrored to WASM):\n- `WEB_SEARCH_RRF_K = 60` (33), `WEB_SEARCH_CONCURRENCY_PER_CATEGORY = 5` (40), `WEB_SEARCH_PROVIDER_LIMIT = 10` (44)\n- `ProviderCategory` (48), `ProviderSpec` (69), `WEB_SEARCH_PROVIDER_REGISTRY` (90), `WEB_SEARCH_PROVIDERS` (327)\n- `default_search_plan_ids()` (339), `build_request_evidence(query, language)` (351), `reciprocal_rank_fusion(entries, k)` (396), `parse_rrf_input` (446), `serialize_rrf_output` (485)\n- WASM exports mirror these in `src/web/wasm-worker/src/lib.rs:237-461`.\n- Intent detection lives in `src/solver_handlers/web_search_intent.rs` (`web_search_query_for` at 207, `extract_web_search_request` at 106); live HTTP fetch handler in `src/solver_handlers/web_requests.rs:23 try_http_fetch`.\n\n## 2. The multi-turn tool-calling loop and planner\n\nTwo layers, cleanly separated.\n\n**Outer loop (client/driver side)** — `driver.rs:128 run_agentic_task_in(task, config)`:\n- `MAX_TURNS: usize = 12` (line 38) — hard cap. Comment says \"the recipe needs five\".\n- `loop` at line 145: cap check → build `ChatCompletionRequest` → `create_chat_completion_with_solver` → if `finish_reason == \"tool_calls\"` execute each call via `execute_tool_call`, push `DriverToolStep`, append assistant turn then `tool` result messages (ordering matters — planner maps `tool_call_id` back to a *prior* assistant turn); otherwise return the final answer.\n- Outcome types: `DriverToolStep` (42), `DriverOutcome` (53) with `turns` and `hit_turn_cap`; `transcript()` (69) and `session_json()` (95).\n\n**Inner planner (server side, stateless)** — `/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784459807581/src/agentic_coding/planner.rs`:\n- `plan_chat_step(messages, tool_names) -> Option<AgenticPlan>` (line 149) is the entry point. It's a *re-derivation-from-transcript* planner, not a stateful state machine: every turn it rescans the whole message history.\n- `AgenticPlan` (53): `ToolCalls(Vec<PlannedToolCall>)` | `Final(String)`. `PlannedToolCall { tool, arguments }` (62).\n- `Capability` enum (77): `Search, Fetch, Read, Write, Edit, Run, Grep, Glob, ListDir, Todo, Subagent, ReadMany, MultiEdit`. `permission_key()` (105) maps to `tool:capability:*` grants; `registry_id()` (140) maps to canonical names. `tool_capability(name)` (145) → `classify_tool` (913) → `capability_router::classify_tool`. Same function drives both planning and the permission gate, deliberately.\n- `Progress` struct (790) + `Progress::scan(messages)` (801): replays the transcript into `completed: Vec<Capability>`, `fetched_text`, `fetched_pages: Vec<(String,String)>`, `search_output`, `run_output`, `fetch_result`. `done(capability)` (855). `result_capability` (918) and `result_tool_call` (929) resolve a tool result back to its originating call; `fetch_call_url` (938) pulls `url` out of the call arguments.\n- Route order in `plan_chat_step` is a priority chain (literal write → learning report → code artifact → self-heal → … ). Web research is dispatched at **planner.rs:309-310**.\n\n**The search → fetch → synthesize planner itself** — `/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784459807581/src/agentic_coding/web_research.rs`:\n- `web_research_query_for(messages)` (17): extracts the query — seed imperative subject, else `solver_handlers::detect_web_search_query`, else \"ends with `?` and `FormalAiEngine` says `unknown`/`web_search`\" → open-world lookup. Resolves pronoun/context references via `is_context_reference` (301) + `topic_from_history` (315).\n- `plan_web_research_step(messages, tool_names, query)` (60) — **this is the three-stage recipe**, expressed as guards on `Progress`:\n  1. `progress.done(Fetch)` → `Final(final_answer(...))`\n  2. `progress.done(Search)` → emit **parallel** `Fetch` calls, one per URL from `research_urls(search_output)`\n  3. otherwise → single `Search` call with `{\"query\": query}`\n- So the \"turns\" for research are effectively **3** (search, fetch-batch, final), inside the 12-turn driver cap. `MAX_RESEARCH_SOURCES = 3` (259) bounds fan-out per round; there is no repeated/iterative deepening loop.\n\nA separate, simpler single-shot route exists in `src/agentic_coding/intent_router.rs`: `plan_web_search_step` (53) and the fetch variant above it (~line 20-46), which just render the raw tool result via `tool_result::render`. It also has a `tool_search` discovery fallback when no search tool is advertised (lines 59-70).\n\n## 3. Synthesis with citations\n\nAll in `web_research.rs`:\n- `final_answer(query, progress)` (100) — **the synthesis step.** If `fetched_pages` is non-empty (the multi-source path), it maps each `(url, evidence)` to `\"{extract}\\n\\n{source_label}: {url}\"` and joins with blank lines — i.e. one cited block per source. Otherwise it falls back to single-source: evidence from `fetched_text` or `search_output`, with a single citation appended via `preferred_url`. Empty → `render_seed_text(\"web_research_no_content\", \"query\", query)`.\n- `extract_answer(query, evidence)` (143) — the extractive summarizer. Under `VERBATIM_EVIDENCE_LIMIT = 600` chars (94) it returns verbatim; above it splits via `crate::summarization::formalize`, scores each sentence, keeps the top `EXTRACT_SENTENCES = 3` (98), then **restores document order** so it reads as prose. No-overlap fallback truncates to the head.\n- `relevance(query, sentence)` (190) — `probability::symbolic_cosine_similarity`, falling back to `character_overlap` (204) for CJK (whitespace tokenization scores Han text 0.0).\n- Citation label comes from seed data: `seed_text(\"web_research_source_label\")` (233) / `render_seed_text` (239). No natural-language literals in this module by design.\n- URL ranking: `research_urls` (261) dedups, promotes the first authoritative host to front, truncates to 3; `authoritative_host` (283) accepts `.gov`, `.edu`, `.gov.uk`; `preferred_url` (251) is now just `research_urls().next()`.\n\n## 4. PR #795 / commit ff7f2600\n\n`feat: triangulate web research and ingest capture JSON` — 17 files, +1126/-56. Two independent features:\n\n**(a) Triangulation — multiple sources instead of one**\n- `src/agentic_coding/planner.rs` (+23/-4): added `Progress.fetched_pages: Vec<(String, String)>` (url, text pairs). `Progress::scan` now, for each successful fetch result, resolves the originating call and records `(url, text)`. Extracted `result_tool_call` (also **fixed a latent bug**: added `.rev()` so the *most recent* matching `tool_call_id` wins) and added `fetch_call_url`.\n- `src/agentic_coding/web_research.rs` (+54/-13): `plan_web_research_step` now emits a `Vec<PlannedToolCall>` — one fetch per URL — instead of `plan_one(tool, fetch_arguments(&url))`. Added `MAX_RESEARCH_SOURCES = 3` and `research_urls()` (dedup + authoritative-first + truncate); `preferred_url` reduced to `research_urls().next()`. `final_answer` gained the `fetched_pages` branch that produces one cited extract per source.\n\n**(b) Web-capture JSON ingestion**\n- `src/shared_dialog.rs` (+110): new `SharedDialogFormat::WebCaptureJson` variant; `detect_format` sniffs `{` + `\"provider\"` + `\"turns\"` + `\"diagnostics\"`; new `parse_web_capture_json` (requires `status == \"ok\"`, else surfaces `diagnostics.unsupportedReason`/`message`) and `capture_diagnostic(intent, values)` which renders messages from seed data rather than hardcoded English.\n- `src/cli_shared_dialog.rs` (+5/-2): CLI enum value `web-capture-json` with aliases `web-capture`, `capture-json`.\n\n**Supporting**: `.github/workflows/release.yml` (+9); `data/seed/closure-generated-04.lino` (+50) and `data/seed/multilingual-responses.lino` (+32) — the new seed strings; `data/meta/self-ast.lino` (+79/-…); `experiments/issue-781/raw-data/chatgpt-web-capture.json` (+506 fixture); `experiments/agent_cli_e2e/run_issue_781.sh` (+80); tests: `tests/unit/issue_781.rs` (+114, new), `tests/unit/shared_dialog.rs` (+53), `tests/integration/formal_ai_cli.rs` (+45), `tests/unit/mod.rs` (+1).\n\n## 5. Knowledge network / links / graph structures\n\nYes — this is the project's core. Links Notation (`.lino`) doublet graphs.\n\n**`/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784459807581/src/link_store.rs`** (571 lines) — the storage boundary:\n- `DoubletLink { index, from, to }` (23) — a single edge in the canonical `from -> to` projection. This is the atomic unit: a *doublet*, the classic two-pointer link.\n- `LinkRecord { stable_id, schema_version, record_type, source_id, links: Vec<DoubletLink> }` (31) — a content-addressed record plus its reducible doublet projection.\n- `LinkStoreBackend` (41): `LinoProjection | DoubletsRs | DoubletsWeb`; `selected_link_store_backend()` (87), `default_native_link_store()` (107). Native builds use the `doublets-rs` crate behind the `doublets-native` feature; browser builds mirror to IndexedDB (`src/web/memory.js`).\n- `LinkStoreError` (49): `IllFormedLinksNotation | Backend`; `validate_memory_links_notation(text)` (121).\n- Bridging: `memory_events_to_link_records(events)` (145), `memory_event_to_link_record(event, sequence)` (155).\n- `DoubletsLinkStore` (290): `new()` (300), `from_links_notation(text)` (312), `events()` (320), `len()`/`is_empty()` (326/332), `native_link_count()` (338), `try_import_links_notation` (260), `try_replace_from_links_notation` (265), `link_records()` (278).\n\n**`/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784459807581/src/links_query.rs`** (528 lines) — a graph query language:\n- `LinksQuery` (39), `NodePattern` (49), `EdgePattern` (55), `Filter` (62), `Field` (71), `FilterOp` (79), `LinksQueryResult` (106) with `to_links_notation()` (116/149).\n- `parse_links_query(query)` (201), `run_links_query(query)` (181), `run_links_query_against(...)` (189).\n\n**`/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784459807581/src/links_format.rs`** (132) — serialization: `format_lino_record(id, pairs)` (9), `format_lino_value{,_verbatim}` (68/41), `push_lino_node` (74), `sanitize_lino_value` (100), `flatten_lino_value` (127).\n\n**`/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784459807581/src/memory.rs`** — the event log that projects into links: `MemoryEvent` (59), `MemoryStore` (112) with `from_events` (125), `append` (132), `import` (139), `record_access` (197), `apply_substitution` (220), `export_links_notation` (263), `import_links_notation` (274), `replace_from_links_notation` (268), file load/save (280/293). Free functions `export_links_notation(events)` (354) and `parse_links_notation(text)` (413).\n\n**\"Associative\" layer** — `/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784459807581/src/associative_package.rs`: `AssociativePackage` (57) is the unit of learned behavior — `PackageHandler` (29), `PackageTrigger` (38), `PackageDependency` (22), `PackagePermission` (48). API: `new` (196), `from_compiled_skill` (209), builder methods `with_dependency`/`with_handler`/`with_trigger`/`with_permission` (261/270/276/282), `replay(prompt) -> Option<PackageReplay>` (297), `links_notation()` (319) ↔ `from_links_notation()` (368), `grants_capability(capability)` (426), `link_records()` (433). `PackageStore` (93): `install` (510), `replay` (532), `permission_for_capability` (539), `permission_for_tool` (556). `default_associative_packages()` (567).\n\nAlso relevant: `src/associative_persistence.rs`, `src/knowledge.rs` (`KnowledgeSource` 78, `OracleSnippet` 153, `CodingOracle` 238 with `lookup`/`knows_language`/`languages`/`cached_count`), `src/self_source_graph.rs`, `src/agentic_coding/source_graph.rs`, `src/agentic_coding/associative_learning.rs`, `src/concepts.rs`.\n\nNote the connective tissue relevant to your interest: the permission model in `Capability::permission_key()` resolves against `PackageStore::permission_for_capability` — so tool authorization is itself a link/associative-package lookup, not a hardcoded table.\n\n## 6. Product / option / constraint modeling\n\n**There is essentially none in the product-decision sense.** No `Product`, `Option`, `Requirement`, `Criterion`, `Alternative`, or `Tradeoff` types exist. The only near-hit is `CandidateSkill` in `src/skill_ledger.rs:141`, which is about skill selection, not product choice.\n\nWhat does exist is **constraint solving at the logic level** — `/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784459807581/src/proof_engine/`:\n- `decision.rs` + `decision/sat.rs` (SAT), `decision/boolean.rs`, `decision/linear.rs` + `decision/linear/proofs.rs` (linear arithmetic decision procedure with proof output)\n- plus `arithmetic.rs`, `library.rs`, `presenter.rs`, `types.rs`\n\nThat's a propositional/linear-arithmetic decision engine, not a product-configuration or multi-criteria-decision model. If you're adding option/constraint modeling, `proof_engine/decision/linear.rs` is the natural substrate to build on, and `LinkRecord`/`DoubletLink` is the natural representation.\n\nOne thing worth flagging beyond what you asked: the entire agentic web path resolves against `corpus.rs`'s fixed offline corpus, so `plan_web_research_step`'s triangulation logic — including the new `MAX_RESEARCH_SOURCES` fan-out from PR #795 — has never actually been exercised against real multi-host search results in this repo. `research_urls` promotes `.gov`/`.edu`/`.gov.uk` hosts, but the corpus only ever contains `ru.wikisource.org` and `wikidata.org` URLs, so the `authoritative_host` branch is dead in practice under the driver. Whether that matters depends on whether a real CLI (the `@link-assistant/agent` integration the `fetch_arguments` comments reference) drives the same planner over live tools — the planner is transport-agnostic, so it would.",
