[2026-07-19T11:27:02.291Z] [INFO]         "text": "This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n\n   The user's single genuine message was: *\"Issue to solve: https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/781 / Your prepared branch: issue-781-c52371d60a25 / Your prepared working directory: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784459807581 / Your prepared Pull Request: https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/795 / New comments on the pull request: 1 / Pull request description was edited after last commit / Merge status is UNSTABLE (non-passing commit status) / Failed pull request checks: 1 / Continue.\"*\n\n   This directs me to continue work on PR #795: address the new PR comment and fix the failing check.\n\n   **Issue #781 itself** is a bug report from an agentic session (Russian): *\"Найди мне зарядку для ноутбука Acer Aspire 3 A325-45 на amazon.in\"* — the assistant failed with `StatusCode: non 2xx status code (403 GET https://shopozz.ru/items/...)`.\n\n   **The new PR comment from konard (2026-07-19T11:09:59Z) is the dominant driver of remaining work.** It requests (paraphrased faithfully):\n   - Deepen the analysis and fully implement the vision from the issue using **auto learning**, and execute the same task using Formal AI via the **Agent CLI**.\n   - Do **deep research** using web search / web fetch with **multi-turn tool calling**.\n   - **Priority order**: first find the original/authentic DC adapter; then search all official sources for compatible manufacturers; only if everything fails, find compatible fallback options (generic DC adapter with compatible characteristics); if the port itself is unavailable, try conversion adapters.\n   - Do this by building an **associative links network (not a neural net)** — a knowledge network with all facts and possible options.\n   - Provide **all** options, not only the most expensive charger+adapters bundle — including options composed of **2 separate items** (conversion adapter + charger); **list cheaper options first by default**.\n   - Everything must be solved by **generalization**, not specific to chargers — any product with any constraints; widest possible range of cases.\n   - Follow contributing guidelines, testing guidelines, vision, roadmap. Cover the most ambitious requirements through generalization, advancing the meta algorithm to its highest potential. Fix anything obsolete or contradicting generalization.\n   - Architecture changes are explicitly permitted anywhere touched.\n   - Plan and execute everything in this **single pull request**, continuing indefinitely until every requirement is fully addressed.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Formal AI / symbolic GOFAI**: associative links network as the AI; no neural weights; Links Notation (`.lino`) doublet graphs; semantic networks.\n   - **Doublets / Links Data Store**: `doublets-rs` native, `doublets-web`/IndexedDB browser.\n   - **\"Data is the interface\"**: behavior, vocabulary, tools driven by `data/seed/*.lino`, not code literals.\n   - **Universal 11-step problem-solving algorithm** (impulse → formalization → context → history → decomposition → TDD test gen → synthesis → combination → verification → simplification → presentation).\n   - **Symbolic world models** (issue #649): `Context`, `Action`, `difference`, `predict`, `merge_from`, `split_off`, `WorldModel`.\n   - **Agentic planner**: stateless re-derivation from transcript; `Capability` enum; `Progress::scan`; `AgenticPlan::{ToolCalls, Final}`.\n   - **Offline deterministic corpus** for `web_search`/`web_fetch` in the in-repo driver (CI has no network).\n   - **Relative meta logic / statement probabilities**, `proof_engine/decision/linear.rs` (linear arithmetic decision procedure).\n   - **Repo gates**: file-size (src ≤1000 lines, warn 900; tests ≤1500, warn 1400), hardcoded-natural-language lint, worker line budget, WASM size, changelog fragment, clippy `-D warnings`, `cargo fmt --check`, total-closure audit.\n   - **Playwright E2E** for the local web app and GitHub Pages; Agent CLI E2E (`@link-assistant/agent`) against `formal-ai serve`.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   - **`src/agentic_coding/web_research.rs`** (371 lines) — *the core file to modify.* Read in full. Current 3-stage recipe:\n     ```rust\n     pub(super) fn plan_web_research_step(\n         messages: &[ChatMessage], tool_names: &[&str], query: &str,\n     ) -> Option<AgenticPlan> {\n         let progress = Progress::scan(messages);\n         if progress.done(Capability::Fetch) {\n             return Some(AgenticPlan::Final(final_answer(query, &progress)));\n         }\n         if progress.done(Capability::Search) {\n             if let Some(tool) = tool_for(tool_names, Capability::Fetch) {\n                 if let Some(output) = progress.search_output.as_deref() {\n                     let calls = research_urls(output).into_iter()\n                         .map(|url| PlannedToolCall { tool: tool.to_owned(), arguments: fetch_arguments(&url) })\n                         .collect::<Vec<_>>();\n                     if !calls.is_empty() { return Some(AgenticPlan::ToolCalls(calls)); }\n                 }\n             }\n             return Some(AgenticPlan::Final(final_answer(query, &progress)));\n         }\n         tool_for(tool_names, Capability::Search)\n             .map(|tool| plan_one(tool, json!({ \"query\": query }).to_string()))\n     }\n     ```\n     Other key items: `VERBATIM_EVIDENCE_LIMIT = 600` (line 94), `EXTRACT_SENTENCES = 3` (98), `MAX_RESEARCH_SOURCES = 3` (259), `final_answer` (100), `extract_answer` (143), `relevance` (190), `character_overlap` (204), `research_urls` (261), `authoritative_host` (283), `preferred_url` (251), `seed_text`/`render_seed_text` (233/239), `web_research_query_for` (17), `is_context_reference` (301), `topic_from_history` (315). **No iterative deepening, no constraints, no options, no tiers, no price sorting.**\n\n   - **`src/agentic_coding/planner.rs`** (1000 lines) — read lines 780–920. `Progress` struct at 790 with `completed: Vec<Capability>`, `fetched_text`, `fetched_pages: Vec<(String,String)>`, `search_output`, `run_output`, `fetch_result`, `search_result`. `Progress::scan` (801) ignores results from earlier user turns via `current_turn`. `done()` (855), **`count()` (859) — the round counter I intend to use for multi-turn**. `plan_one` (875), `write_arguments` (888), `fetch_arguments` (905) emits `{\"url\":…, \"format\":\"text\"}`. `plan_chat_step` entry at 149; web research dispatched at 309-310.\n\n   - **`src/world_model.rs`** (716 lines) — *chosen substrate for the new design.* API: `Dependency` (67), `Statement` (102), `Action` (164) with `adding`/`removing`/`id`, `Context` (219) with `assert_link`/`retract_link`/`holds`/`links`/`statements`/`add_statement`/`recalculate`/`apply_action`/`predict` (420)/`difference` (443)/`merge_from`/`split_off`/`links_notation` (515), `ContextDiff` (594) with `is_empty`/`links_notation`, `Prediction` (636), `WorldModel` (669) with `difference`/`predict`/`target_reached`/`commit_current_to_general`.\n\n   - **`src/agentic_coding/corpus.rs`** — offline deterministic corpus. `struct CorpusPage { url, title, keywords: Vec<String>, body }`, `pages()` (33), `web_search` (81), `web_fetch` (112). **Tests must add corpus pages to exercise the flow deterministically.**\n\n   - **`src/agentic_coding/driver.rs`** — `DRIVER_TOOLS` (34), `MAX_TURNS = 12` (38), `run_agentic_task_in` (128), `execute_tool_call` (216), `tool_definitions` (240), `tool_description` (251), `DriverOutcome` (53), `session_json()` (95).\n\n   - **`src/links_format.rs`** — `format_lino_record(id, pairs) -> String` (line 9), `format_lino_value`, `sanitize_lino_value`.\n\n   - **`VISION.md`** (read in full, 289 lines) — mandates associative link network, no neural inference, data-driven seed, library-first availability, single-file reproducibility.\n\n   - **`CONTRIBUTING.md`** (first 140 lines) — the 9 mandatory development rules quoted in the analysis, notably: Agent CLI must author the change; no deferral; prove generality with different wording each time; real Agent-CLI E2E in CI plus one test per requirement and one whole-task test; production code stays general (hardcoded cases only in tests); real logs in case studies; small atomic commits.\n\n   - **`docs/case-studies/issue-781/requirements.md`** — existing R1–R11 trace table (R5 \"Improve Formal AI generally, not with charger-specific phrases\", R6 \"Use recursive/cross-source reasoning\", R11 \"Cover the whole task with automated tests\"). Needs R12+ rows for the new reviewer requirements.\n\n   - **`scripts/check-file-size.rs`** — src `max_lines: 1_000`, `warn_lines: 900`; another profile `max_lines: 1_500`, `warn_lines: 1_400`.\n\n   - **`scripts/check-hardcoded-language.rs`** — was being read when summarization was requested. Scans `src/**/*.rs` for prose literals; fails on new unlisted debt AND on stale allowlist rows. Allowlist at `scripts/hardcoded-language-allowlist.txt`. Design doc: `docs/design/no-hardcoded-natural-language.md`, REQUIREMENTS R379.\n\n   - **`ci-logs/e2e-local-web-app.log`** (1271 lines, downloaded) — failing E2E evidence.\n\n   - **No file has been created or edited yet.** The only repository change so far is the `git merge origin/main --no-edit` merge commit on the branch.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n\n   - **Failing check \"E2E Tests (local web app)\" on run 29680389544.** Failing specs: `tests/issue-153.spec.js:475:3` (\"multilingual information-search phrasings route to web search\", plus retry #1), `tests/issue-282.spec.js:65:5` (\"Hindi unknown prompts use the native Rust stable-id opener\"), `tests/issue-747.spec.js:15:1` (\"multilingual desktop web search works with agent permission off and no local API\"). Assertion errors were `expect(locator).toHaveCount(initial + 2, { timeout: 20_000 })` and a `toContainText` failure. Final tally \"1 failed\".\n     - **Fix applied (not yet verified):** merged `origin/main`, which contains `d832ef41 \"Stabilize browser worker startup and search fallback\"` from merged PR #794 — this targets exactly these web-search-routing/browser-worker startup flakes. The branch had been 12 commits behind main. **Still needs local and/or CI verification.**\n\n   - **Initial log inspection pitfall:** `gh run view --log-failed` output tail was post-job cleanup noise, not the failure. Fixed by grepping the log for `✘|Error:|toHaveCount|failed` markers instead of reading the tail.\n\n   - No user feedback correcting my approach was received (the reviewer comment predates my work in this session).\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n\n   - **Diagnosed the CI failure** to browser-worker/search-fallback flakiness already fixed on `main`; merged main as the root-cause fix rather than patching tests.\n   - **Established the architectural gap**: the reviewer wants constraint-based, tiered, composite, price-sorted option research over an associative links network, and the repo has **zero** product/option/constraint modeling. Confirmed via the Explore agent that no `Product`, `Option`, `Requirement`, `Criterion`, `Alternative`, or `Tradeoff` types exist.\n   - **Selected a reuse-first design** rather than inventing a parallel structure: map the reviewer's ask onto `src/world_model.rs` — target context = requirement constraints, current context = researched facts, `Context::difference` = unresolved constraints (drives the multi-turn loop), `Action` = a purchase option, multi-link Actions = composite (2-item) options, `predict` verifies an option closes the gap. This satisfies \"associative links network, not neural net\" genuinely and reuses existing machinery.\n   - **Identified determinism constraint**: the in-repo agentic driver has no live network, so end-to-end demonstration must add pages to `corpus.rs`; the planner is transport-agnostic so a real Agent CLI with live tools drives the same logic.\n   - **Identified compliance constraints** for new code: ≤1000 lines per src file, no hardcoded user-facing prose in `src/` (must come from seed `.lino`).\n\n6. All user messages:\n\n   - *\"Issue to solve: https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/781\\nYour prepared branch: issue-781-c52371d60a25\\nYour prepared working directory: /tmp/gh-issue-solver-1784459807581\\nYour prepared Pull Request: https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/795\\nNew comments on the pull request: 1\\nPull request description was edited after last commit\\nMerge status is UNSTABLE (non-passing commit status)\\nFailed pull request checks: 1\\nContinue.\"*\n\n   - (Final turn) *\"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools. ... Your task is to create a detailed summary of the conversation so far...\"*\n\n   No security-relevant instructions or constraints were stated by the user in this conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n\n   - **Task #1 — Fix failing E2E check on PR 795.** Merge of `main` done; needs verification (local E2E run and/or fresh CI) and push.\n   - **Task #2 — Design generalized constraint-based option research over links network.** Design chosen (see Current Work); not yet implemented.\n   - **Task #3 — Implement multi-turn deep research loop (search → fetch → refine).** Extend `plan_web_research_step` beyond its single search+fetch round using `Progress::count` as a round counter, within `MAX_TURNS = 12`.\n   - **Task #4 — Add per-requirement + whole-task tests and Agent CLI E2E.** Per CONTRIBUTING rule 6, plus a differently-worded non-charger case to prove generality (rule 4).\n   - Implicit follow-ups: add R12+ rows to `docs/case-studies/issue-781/requirements.md`; add a changelog fragment under `changelog.d/`; update the PR description; verify all local gates (`cargo fmt --all -- --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings`, `cargo test --all-features`, file-size, hardcoded-language, total-closure, worker-line, WASM-size) before pushing; `gh pr ready 795`.\n\n8. Current Work:\n\n   Immediately before the summarization request I was completing pre-implementation reconnaissance for the new option-research architecture. Specifically I had just discovered the two compliance gates that constrain the new module and was reading `scripts/check-hardcoded-language.rs` to learn its exact rules — its doc comment states: *\"every user-facing sentence must come from the seed knowledge base (`data/seed/*.lino`), not from a string literal typed into the engine\"*, and the check fails both when a new unlisted prose literal appears in `src/` and when an allowlist row becomes stale.\n\n   The concrete design settled on (stated in-conversation, not yet written to disk):\n\n   - **`src/option_network.rs`** — general, product-agnostic library module:\n     - `Constraint { attribute, bound }` with `Bound::{Exact(String), Equals{value,unit}, AtLeast{value,unit}}`, fixed-point integers (no floats) for determinism.\n     - `Candidate { id, label, tier, provides: BTreeMap<String, Supply>, offer }`, `Supply::{Nominal(String), Quantity{value,unit}}`.\n     - `Offer { price_minor, currency, seller, url, availability }`.\n     - `Tier`: Authentic → OfficialCompatible → GenericCompatible (research order = tier ascending).\n     - `OptionPlan { items, total_price_minor, currency, satisfies, unmet, tier }` — enumerate **minimal** subsets of size 1..=max_items whose combined provisions satisfy all constraints, so a lone charger is listed when sufficient and \"conversion adapter + charger\" appears when neither alone suffices.\n     - `ranked()` — satisfying plans first, then **total price ascending** (reviewer: \"by default we should list cheaper options first\"), then tier rank, then item count, then id for determinism.\n     - Backed by `world_model::Context`: target context from constraints, current context from researched facts, `difference()` exposing unresolved constraints, `links_notation()` for the auditable projection.\n   - **`src/agentic_coding/option_research.rs`** — the agentic recipe in repo idiom (TASK constant + matcher + `render_document`), driving tiered multi-turn research keyed on the non-empty `ContextDiff`.\n   - **`data/seed/option-research.lino`** — tier vocabulary and multilingual (`en|ru|hi|zh`) attribute names, keeping all natural language out of `src/`.\n\n   Also in flight: the background release build `cargo build --release --bin formal-ai` (log `ci-logs/build-release.log`, background ID `bbte2bra7`) was still compiling (`lindera v3.0.7`, `meta-language v0.45.0`) and had not produced `target/release/formal-ai`.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n\n   Finish reading `scripts/check-hardcoded-language.rs` rules, then write `src/option_network.rs` — the general constraint/option/composite-plan engine layered on `src/world_model.rs` — with unit tests, keeping the file under the 900-line warn threshold and free of user-facing prose literals.\n\n   This is directly in line with Task #2, which I created as: *\"Design generalized constraint-based option research over links network — Per reviewer comment: build an associative links network (facts + options), not charger-specific. Must generalize to any product with any constraints. Tiers: authentic/original -> official compatible -> generic compatible -> composite (conversion adapter + charger). List ALL options, cheapest first.\"*\n\n   My stated design rationale immediately before the summary request was: *\"`world_model` is a strong fit — the reviewer's ask maps onto it directly: target context = requirement, difference = unresolved constraints (drives multi-turn research), Action = a purchase option, composite options = multi-link actions.\"*\n\n   Before pushing, Task #1 also still needs closing: confirm the `origin/main` merge actually clears the \"E2E Tests (local web app)\" failure (fresh CI run on the merged commit).\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/box/.claude/projects/-tmp-gh-issue-solver-1784459807581/171c0084-85f0-47d7-a986-6f93ae4aeef7.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."
