[2026-07-19T12:22:36.497Z] [INFO]         "content": "        run: experiments/agent_cli_e2e/run_agent_cli.sh\n\n      - name: \"Run agent CLI E2E — capability-first local code search (issue #758)\"\n        env:\n          PORT: 8782\n        run: experiments/agent_cli_e2e/run_issue_758.sh\n\n      - name: \"Run agent CLI E2E — generated programs use harness commands (issue #716)\"\n        # The exact screenshot reproduction must create the source in the real\n        # Agent CLI workspace, then ask that harness to compile and run it. The\n        # request trace preserves both shell calls so a prose-only response or\n        # server-private execution cannot satisfy this check.\n        env:\n          PORT: 8776\n          TASK: \"Give me hello world program in Rust\"\n          EXPECT_FILE: main.rs\n          EXPECT_TEXT: \"Hello, world!\"\n          MIN_POSTS: 4\n          EXPECT_SERVER_TEXTS: |-\n            rustc main.rs -o main\n            ./main\n        run: experiments/agent_cli_e2e/run_agent_cli.sh\n\n      - name: \"Run agent CLI E2E — auto-learn client execution architecture (issue #716)\"\n        # Replay the same investigation through Formal AI's associative-memory\n        # adapter and real Agent CLI tools. The report remains review-gated; its\n        # evidence links make the architectural promotion auditable.\n        env:\n          PORT: 8777\n          TASK: \"Use Formal AI auto-learning to inspect the persisted issue 716 client-execution failures as an associative links network, rank the observations and architectural amendments, keep promotion human-review gated, and write client-execution-learning-report.lino.\"\n          EXPECT_FILE: client-execution-learning-report.lino\n          EXPECT_TEXT: \"lesson:typed-execution-artifact\"\n          MIN_POSTS: 3\n        run: experiments/agent_cli_e2e/run_agent_cli.sh\n\n      - name: \"Run agent CLI E2E — declarative new-file phrasing (issue #712)\"\n        # The exact declarative shape from issue #712 previously fell through to\n        # the read router. The live CLI must execute the complete write plan and\n        # leave the requested file behind, proving this is more than a response-\n        # serialization fix.\n        env:\n          PORT: 8776\n          TASK: \"new file: notes.txt, contents: hello\"\n          EXPECT_FILE: notes.txt\n          EXPECT_TEXT: hello\n          MIN_POSTS: 4\n        run: experiments/agent_cli_e2e/run_agent_cli.sh\n\n      - name: \"Run agent CLI E2E — report action executes gh (issue #714)\"\n        timeout-minutes: 3\n        env:\n          PORT: 8780\n        run: experiments/issue_714_agentic_mode/run_report_e2e.sh\n\n      - name: \"Run agent CLI E2E — research, report, recall, and learn (issue #687)\"\n        # Continue four natural-language turns in one real Agent CLI session.\n        # A PATH-local fake gh proves shell execution without mutating GitHub.\n        env:\n          PORT: 8776\n        run: experiments/agent_cli_e2e/run_issue_687.sh\n\n      - name: \"Run agent CLI E2E — filed report stays readable and bounded (issue #771)\"\n        # The reported session answered a question from a whole scraped page and\n        # then filed it, producing a 51KB issue whose transcript escaped its own\n        # markdown. Asserts over the real transport that every turn stays inside\n        # an attributed block and the body fits GitHub's issue size limit.\n        env:\n          PORT: 8781\n        run: experiments/agent_cli_e2e/run_issue_771.sh\n\n      - name: \"Run agent CLI E2E — compatibility research triangulates sources (issue #781)\"\n        # A real marketplace compatibility question must not stop after the\n        # first result. The server trace proves one search fans out to at least\n        # three fetches and the real Agent CLI executes each one. Deterministic\n        # coverage checks the following synthesis round and its citations.\n        env:\n          PORT: 8783\n        run: experiments/agent_cli_e2e/run_issue_781.sh\n\n      - name: \"Run agent CLI E2E — auto-learning across two harnesses (issue #715)\"\n        # The derived report names its own promotion gate",
