[2026-07-19T12:36:21.129Z] [INFO]         "content": "127\tfn plan_deeper_round(tool_names: &[&str], progress: &Progress, query: &str) -> Option<AgenticPlan> {\n128\t    if progress.count(Capability::Search) >= MAX_RESEARCH_ROUNDS {\n129\t        return None;\n130\t    }\n131\t    let open = uncovered_aspects(query, progress);\n132\t    // A refinement has to actually refine. Nothing uncovered means the question\n133\t    // is answered; *everything* uncovered means the evidence bears on none of it\n134\t    // — usually because the sources answer in another language than the question\n135\t    // was asked in — and re-issuing the same terms would return the same pages.\n136\t    // Requiring a proper subset rules both out, and makes the loop terminate on\n137\t    // its own: uncovered aspects only ever shrink as evidence accumulates.\n138\t    if open.is_empty() || open.len() >= aspects_of(query).len() {\n139\t        return None;\n140\t    }\n141\t    let tool = tool_for(tool_names, Capability::Search)?;\n142\t    Some(plan_one(\n143\t        tool,\n144\t        json!({ \"query\": open.join(\" \") }).to_string(),\n145\t    ))\n146\t}\n147\t\n148\t/// The aspects of `query` that no fetched page supports.\n149\t///\n150\t/// This is the loop's open-question signal, and it carries no vocabulary: an\n151\t/// aspect is a content token of the question, and it is covered when some page\n152\t/// actually mentions it. That is deliberately the same symbolic, non-neural\n153\t/// notion of aboutness [`relevance`] ranks sentences with, applied to the\n154\t/// question instead of the answer.\n155\t///\n156\t/// Scripts that do not space-separate words tokenize to one long token, which\n157\t/// would report the whole question uncovered forever. For those the aspect is\n158\t/// the ideograph, matching the fallback [`relevance`] already uses.\n159\tfn uncovered_aspects(query: &str, progress: &Progress) -> Vec<String> {\n160\t    if progress.fetched_pages.is_empty() {\n161\t        return Vec::new();"
