[2026-07-19T12:36:30.986Z] [INFO]           "old_string": "    let open = uncovered_aspects(query, progress);\n    // A refinement has to actually refine. Nothing uncovered means the question\n    // is answered; *everything* uncovered means the evidence bears on none of it\n    // — usually because the sources answer in another language than the question\n    // was asked in — and re-issuing the same terms would return the same pages.\n    // Requiring a proper subset rules both out, and makes the loop terminate on\n    // its own: uncovered aspects only ever shrink as evidence accumulates.\n    if open.is_empty() || open.len() >= aspects_of(query).len() {\n        return None;\n    }",
[2026-07-19T12:36:30.986Z] [INFO]           "new_string": "    let open = uncovered_aspects(query, progress);\n    // A refinement has to actually refine, and the bar for spending another\n    // round has to be high, because token coverage is a weak proxy for\n    // \"answered\". A page that genuinely answers \"when are elections in usa\"\n    // still will not repeat every word of the question, so a few uncovered\n    // tokens are normal and must not trigger a second search.\n    //\n    // Another round is therefore justified only when the evidence covers most of\n    // the question and leaves a distinct minority of it open — the shape of a\n    // real follow-up, where the specs were found and only the warranty is\n    // missing. At the other extreme, *everything* uncovered means the evidence\n    // bears on none of the question, usually because the sources answer in a\n    // different language than it was asked in; re-issuing those same terms would\n    // return the same pages. Both extremes stop here.\n    //\n    // This also makes the loop terminate on its own, independently of the round\n    // budget: uncovered aspects only ever shrink as evidence accumulates.\n    if open.is_empty() || open.len() * 2 >= aspects_of(query).len() {\n        return None;\n    }"
